    {
      "id": "gp60yd",
      "label": "demo_movetransition",
      "bg": null,
      "music": null,
      "events": [
        {
          "id": "toxhiu",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The most common MoveTransition is move, which slides around images that have changed position on the screen."
        },
        {
          "id": "vqxwlc",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "huceg0",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "move",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "w5i9i9",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Just like that."
        },
        {
          "id": "dhgaek",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "example moveinout",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "2dxwny",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: There are also the moveout and movein transitions."
        },
        {
          "id": "doq2ke",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The moveout transitions (moveoutleft, moveoutright, moveouttop, and moveoutbottom) slide hidden images off the appropriate side of the screen."
        },
        {
          "id": "podko1",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The movein transitions (moveinleft, moveinright, moveintop, and moveinbottom) slide in new images."
        },
        {
          "id": "4z0ffi",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Let's see them all in action."
        },
        {
          "id": "5mfruu",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide example",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "o36yl0",
          "type": "wait",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "sq2puu",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide eileen happy",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "gj00wn",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveoutleft",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "vso9ck",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "yh8m9d",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveinbottom",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "imf431",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide eileen happy",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "5ryc1l",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveoutbottom",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "cdt3ib",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "spqudb",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveinright",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "alhodp",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide eileen happy",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "x4ix6l",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveoutright",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "z14897",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "show eileen happy:"
        },
        {
          "id": "x99ngh",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveintop",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "xbeozo",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide eileen happy",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "5xvdu8",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveouttop",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "rjot24",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "npwuyy",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveinleft",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "8xhqll",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: That's it for the moveins and moveouts."
        },
        {
          "id": "1n9ixq",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Finally, there are the zoomin and zoomout transitions, which show and hide things using a zoom."
        },
        {
          "id": "p8uhoy",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide eileen happy",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "p9xbgl",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "zoomout",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "6rlq4b",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "zxvgl8",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "zoomin",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "n9914m",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: And that's all there is."
        },
        {
          "id": "ift6pu",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide example",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "u42bm5",
          "type": "wait",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "176p21",
          "type": "jump",
          "scene_id": null,
          "_isReturn": true
        }
      ],
      "scene_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5tyxig",
      "label": "demo_alphadissolve",
      "bg": "bg washington",
      "music": null,
      "events": [
        {
          "id": "u8dlpd",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The AlphaDissolve transition lets you use one displayable to combine two others. Click, and I'll show you an example."
        },
        {
          "id": "6rl15z",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "black"
        },
        {
          "id": "s9qbc0",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "dissolve",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "r3biib",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "bg washington"
        },
        {
          "id": "mwe9et",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "k5hi75",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "alpha_example",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "tuc1mn",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The AlphaDissolve displayable takes a control displayable, usually an ATL transform."
        },
        {
          "id": "b1p4qt",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "alpha_control",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "gfy2eq",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: To be useful, the control displayable should be partially transparent."
        },
        {
          "id": "d412mu",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: During an AlphaDissolve, the old screen is used to fill the transparent areas of the image, while the new screen fills the opaque areas."
        },
        {
          "id": "q0qpee",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "black"
        },
        {
          "id": "r104hv",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: For our spotlight example, the old screen is this all-black image."
        },
        {
          "id": "zqbmgm",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "bg washington"
        },
        {
          "id": "tquwe9",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "9voytc",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The new screen is me just standing here."
        },
        {
          "id": "saxu8y",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "black"
        },
        {
          "id": "57lphx",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "dissolve",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "rt9p3e",
          "type": "bg",
          "bg": "bg washington"
        },
        {
          "id": "sddl08",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "eileen happy",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "0wbzv2",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "alpha_example",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "135j2l",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: By combining them using AlphaDissolve, we can build a complicated effect out of simpler parts."
        },
        {
          "id": "9vdif4",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide example",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "pz6hwc",
          "type": "wait",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "kwfkh3",
          "type": "jump",
          "scene_id": null,
          "_isReturn": true
        },
        {
          "id": "mp901e",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "language: japanese-strict"
        },
        {
          "id": "w8ex1j",
          "type": "jump",
          "scene_id": "yur1tj",
          "transition": "none",
          "_targetLabel": "translations"
        }
      ],
      "scene_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "yur1tj",
      "label": "translations",
      "bg": null,
      "music": null,
      "events": [
        {
          "id": "g2u1z2",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Ren'Py includes support for translating your game into languages other than the one it was originally written in."
        },
        {
          "id": "zy54dg",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: This includes the translation of every string in the game, including dialogue, menu choice, and interface strings, and of images and other assets."
        },
        {
          "id": "wfb4tc",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: While Ren'Py can find dialogue and menu choice strings for you, you'll have to indicate which other strings need translation."
        },
        {
          "id": "ekft35",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "example characters",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "2q1b5g",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: For example, here is how we define a character and her name."
        },
        {
          "id": "gsh7ca",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "example characters showtrans",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "gcmze3",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: To mark Lucy's name as translatable, we surround it by parentheses preceded by a single underscore."
        },
        {
          "id": "telu74",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Notice how we don't translate the reddish color that we use for her name. That stays the same for all languages."
        },
        {
          "id": "wnqbot",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide example",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "u385mt",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "launcher translate at launcher_place",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "gp74hr",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveinleft",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "wk80iy",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Once that's done, you can generate the translation files. That's done by going to the launcher, and clicking translate."
        },
        {
          "id": "e1mcga",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: After you type in the name of the language you'll be translating to, choosing Generate Translations will scan your game and create translation files."
        },
        {
          "id": "d9ocm2",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The files will be generated in game/tl/language, where language is the name of the language you typed in."
        },
        {
          "id": "o1w3nv",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: You'll need to edit those files to include translations for everything in your game."
        },
        {
          "id": "4b9a41",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: If you want to localize image files, you can also place them in game/tl/language."
        },
        {
          "id": "mpf4ws",
          "type": "raw",
          "raw_code": "hide launcher",
          "_isSkipped": true
        },
        {
          "id": "cv3h3b",
          "type": "effect",
          "kind": "moveoutleft",
          "dur": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "xqnp7i",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "example translate_font large",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "2jonbi",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: If the default fonts used by the game do not support the language you are translating to, you will have to change them."
        },
        {
          "id": "m7jo7s",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The translate python statement can be used to set the values of gui variables to change the font."
        },
        {
          "id": "7ipnq0",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The translate style statement sets style properties more directly."
        },
        {
          "id": "fnur4c",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: If you need to add new files, such as font files, you can place them into the game/tl/language directory where Ren'Py will find them."
        },
        {
          "id": "gxxnic",
          "type": "image",
          "image": "example language_picker large",
          "side": "center"
        },
        {
          "id": "se90p7",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Finally, you'll have to add support for picking the language of the game. That usually goes into the preferences screen, found in screens.rpy."
        },
        {
          "id": "qhayjy",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: Here's an excerpt of the preferences screen of this tutorial. The Language action tells Ren'Py to change the language. It takes a string giving a language name, or None."
        },
        {
          "id": "p7mb8r",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "e: The None language is special, as it's the default language that the visual novel was written in. Since this tutorial was written in English, Language(None) selects English."
        },
        {
          "id": "ln6079",
          "type": "jump",
          "scene_id": null,
          "_isReturn": true
        },
        {
          "id": "xpi447",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "\""
        },
        {
          "id": "hem2wp",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "\""
        },
        {
          "id": "1qql7f",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "\""
        },
        {
          "id": "bpk3m9",
          "type": "narration",
          "text": "\""
        },
        {
          "id": "oj60x5",
          "type": "jump",
          "scene_id": "zqu60l",
          "transition": "none",
          "_targetLabel": "start"
        }
      ],
      "scene_ids": []
    },
    {
      "id": "zqu60l",
